;; Which changes make CI run driver tests. Read by `mage.modules` (which decides), by
;; `metabase.core.modules-test` (which checks the exemptions are still justified), and by
;; `dev.deps-graph/module-boundary-stats` (which counts the result).
;;
;; `:trigger-modules` and `:cloud-trigger-modules` are the roots: a change to one of these, or to anything
;; they transitively depend on, runs driver tests. The cloud set additionally pulls in the drivers that
;; need secrets and network round trips.
;;
;; `:exempt-modules` are the modules upstream of a root that we have decided not to trigger on anyway.
;; Every entry is an unverified bet that the coupling is not real enough to break a driver test. The
;; set should only shrink: its size is a module-boundary ratchet (`:driver-test-exempt-modules`), and
;; `metabase.core.modules-test` fails any entry the graph no longer justifies (not a declared module,
;; or no longer upstream of a driver-triggering module). Dropping an entry restores those driver-test
;; runs, so watch it against `:driver-test-triggering-modules`, which counts what is left after the
;; exemptions apply and moves the other way.
{:trigger-modules
 #{driver transforms}

 :cloud-trigger-modules
 #{query-processor transforms
   enterprise/transforms enterprise/transforms-python}

 :exempt-modules
 #{analytics
   analytics-interface
   api
